  "database": "rschema_0163",
  "question": "A sugar cane planting management system is mainly used to record and manage sugar cane planting plots, variety information, employee fertilization records, etc., to help agricultural managers effectively manage plots, planting and fertilization operations. The system covers the following core functions to ensure that the entire process from plot management to planting and fertilization is fully recorded and tracked.\nPlot management: including the region, area, soil type, person in charge ID, soil pH, organic matter content. Used to record the basic information of each sugar cane planting plot, including the unique identification of the plot, the geographical location, area, soil type, etc. Each plot is managed by a person in charge, and the person in charge ID is associated with the employee table.\nSugar cane variety management: including variety name, suitable climate, maturity cycle, suitable soil. Record different varieties of sugar cane information, including variety name, suitable climate, maturity cycle and suitable soil type. This table helps managers select suitable sugarcane varieties and make reasonable variety selection according to the conditions of different plots.\nEmployee management: including employee ID, name, gender, working hours, and telephone number. Record the information of each employee involved in sugar cane planting and management, including name, contact information, and working hours. This table is associated with the plot table and fertilization record table to identify the person in charge of the plot and the fertilization operator.\nPlanting record management: including plot ID, variety ID, planting time, planting quantity, planting method, and planter ID. Record the planting situation of each plot, including information such as the sugar cane variety planted, planting time, planting method, and planting quantity. The planter ID is associated with the employee table to identify the specific planting operator.\nFertilization record management: person in charge ID, plot ID, fertilization time, fertilization type, fertilization amount, fertilization method, and remarks. Record the fertilization operation of each plot, including the fertilization time, fertilization type, fertilization amount, and fertilization method. The person in charge ID is associated with the employee to identify the executor of the fertilization operation.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0163\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` varchar(10) NOT NULL,\n  `working_hours` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `telephone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`employee_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sugar_cane_variety` (\n  `variety_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `variety_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `suitable_climate` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `maturity_cycle` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `suitable_soil` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`variety_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `plot` (\n  `plot_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `region` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `area` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `soil_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `person_in_charge_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `soil_ph` decimal(4,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `organic_matter_content` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`plot_id`),\n  KEY `person_in_charge_id` (`person_in_charge_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `plot_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`person_in_charge_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `planting_record` (\n  `planting_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `plot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `variety_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `planting_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `planting_quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `planting_method` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `planter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`planting_record_id`),\n  KEY `plot_id` (`plot_id`),\n  KEY `variety_id` (`variety_id`),\n  KEY `planter_id` (`planter_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `planting_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`plot_id`) REFERENCES `plot` (`plot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `planting_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`variety_id`) REFERENCES `sugar_cane_variety` (`variety_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `planting_record_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`planter_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `fertilization_record` (\n  `fertilization_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `person_in_charge_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `plot_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `fertilization_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `fertilization_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `fertilization_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `fertilization_method` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `remarks` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`fertilization_record_id`),\n  KEY `person_in_charge_id` (`person_in_charge_id`),\n  KEY `plot_id` (`plot_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `fertilization_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`person_in_charge_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`employee_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `fertilization_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`plot_id`) REFERENCES `plot` (`plot_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
